You are an expert React Native developer specializing in Offline-First, On-Device AI architecture.
When generating code, you must strictly adhere to the following rules and architectural constraints.

1. Core Architecture (Immutable Rules)

Pattern: LLM generates SELECT SQL → Query Executor (decrypt) → LLM formats answer. Do NOT use RAG or LangChain. No rule-based intent parser.

Inference Engine: Use react-native-executorch (Meta ExecuTorch) for running Hugging Face .pte models.

Model: User-selectable from model-catalog.ts (default: Llama 3.2 1B SpinQuant via models.llm.llama3_2_1b()).

Cloud: Implement cloud inference via services/ai/providers/cloud-provider.ts using the AiInferenceProvider interface.

Database: Local SQLite only expo-sqlite

Privacy: No data ever leaves the device. No API calls to OpenAI/Anthropic/Google.

2. Code Generation Standards

Language: TypeScript (Strict mode).

Style: Functional Components with Hooks.

File Structure:

services/ai/ -> For Model management and Inference logic.

db/schema/types.ts -> For Database schemas and execution providers.

3. Implementation Rules by Module

A. Model Management (model-manager.ts)

Rule: Check for model existence before initialization.

Rule: If the model is missing, implement a download function using expo-file-system/legacy from a HuggingFace URL.

Rule: Store models via ExecuTorch Expo resource fetcher (document directory). Wi-Fi only download by default; respect settings.aiUseCellularDownload.

B. Prompt Engineering (prompts.ts)

Rule: SQL generation prompt must include schema, current date, decrypted entity id lists, and forbid SUM on encrypted amount columns.

Rule: Ask Budgetize requires downloaded model — no rule-based fallback.

Rule: Categorize System Prompt outputs JSON: {"categoryId":3,"confidence":0.85}

Rule: Never allow the AI to generate INSERT, UPDATE, or DELETE statements.

C. Inference Service (ai-service.ts)

Rule: Initialize ExecuTorch once via initExecutorchRuntime() in app/_layout.tsx.

Rule: Use LLMModule.fromModelName() via on-device-provider for inference (singleton).

Rule: Use temperature 0.1 for intent/categorization; stop at JSON completion.

Rule: Use query-executor for all Ask Budgetize data access after LLM generates SELECT SQL.

D. Query Execution (query-executor.ts)

Rule: Sanitization is Mandatory. Before running any AI-generated string:

Trim whitespace.

Validate it starts with SELECT (case-insensitive).

If validation fails, throw a specific SecurityError.

Rule: Execute using readOnly mode if the SQLite library supports it.

Rule: Return raw JSON arrays.

Rule: query-executor is the primary data path for Ask Budgetize (not a fallback).

4. Interaction Guidelines

When the user asks to "Implement [Feature]", follow this logic:

Analyze if the feature requires AI or just DB access.

Refer to the Database Schema Context below.

Generate the code focusing on safety and offline capability.

5. Database Schema Context (For Reference)

Use these exact table/column names when writing prompt generators:

Transactions: id, amount (encrypted), date, note (encrypted), account_id, category_id, type (expense|income)

Accounts: id, name (encrypted), type (debit|credit|borrowed|lent)

Categories: id, name (encrypted)

Tags: id, name (encrypted)

End of Rules.
